{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789176448357,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_7yz9mBixMe7ZQw6VLxpvZCzt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo"},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo</path>\n<type>directory</type>\n<entries>\n.git/\n.gitignore\n.handwork/\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nsrc/\ntests/\n\n(8 entries)\n</entries>","metadata":{"preview":".git/\n.gitignore\n.handwork/\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nsrc/\ntests/","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"directory","path":"/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo","entries":[".git/",".gitignore",".handwork/","package-lock.json","package.json","README.md","src/","tests/"],"offset":1,"totalEntries":8,"truncated":false}},"title":"","time":{"start":1789176448350,"end":1789176448355}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_019a02918e2f7e78016aa4aa804a5487d1a007e9156f6a2bc4"}},"id":"prt_0933a0559001hZSl3OeORBdvWQ","sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","messageID":"msg_09339ee5b001izg7s6H4fItxCI"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789176448386,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_biO81YRIS19HnbhNKTdiEY5w","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status --short"},"output":"(no output)","metadata":{"output":"(no output)","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git status --short","time":{"start":1789176448366,"end":1789176448385}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_019a02918e2f7e78016aa4aa804a4c87d18ca1fda1c13a2ebb"}},"id":"prt_0933a0557001XOC335gZDWO1HL","sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","messageID":"msg_09339ee5b001izg7s6H4fItxCI"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789176529167,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_10kiZu6ATszTYQpDACLm7Hzk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Inspect project isolation paths","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Inspect repository for project read/update/list endpoints, membership authorization and cache keys/invalidation. Identify relevant files and minimal fixes. Also identify existing test commands. Research only; do not edit. Thoroughness medium."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f6cc5fab0ffeoiJ5JsnUM5uld3\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\nThree defects are evident from static inspection: **missing authorization on project read/update, cross-organization list-cache collisions, and missing list invalidation after updates**. No files were edited; tests were not run.\n\n### Endpoints and authorization\n\nProject routes are registered in [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/routes/projects.ts:10–12](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/routes/projects.ts#L10):\n\n| Endpoint | Current behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /projects/:projectId` | Requires a session, but does **not** check organization membership. |\n| `PATCH /projects/:projectId` | Requires a session; calls the same unchecked detail function before updating. |\n| `GET /organizations/:organizationId/projects` | Checks current membership **before** cache access—correct ordering. |\n\nThe implementation is in [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts:10–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L10).\n\n**Minimal authorization fix:** In `detail`, after the existing missing-project check, call:\n```ts\nrequireMembership(db, userId, project.organizationId);\n```\nBecause `update` already calls `detail`, this protects both operations before body validation, mutation, or cache deletion. Use the stored ownership—not organization IDs supplied in query/body. Keep missing projects returning 404.\n\nRelevant supporting files:\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/auth/session.ts:3–7](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/auth/session.ts#L3): missing/invalid session → 401.\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/auth/membership.ts:4–5](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/auth/membership.ts#L4): nonmember → 403.\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/db/membership-repository.ts:3–7](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/db/membership-repository.ts#L3): live membership lookup and revocation; no authorization cache to invalidate.\n\n### Cache keys and invalidation\n\n**1. List keys omit organization identity.**\n\n[/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/keys.ts:2–3](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/keys.ts#L2) accepts `organizationId` but ignores it:\n```ts\nprojects:list:${page}:${pageSize}:${sort}:${direction}\n```\nConsequently, Alice can populate an org-a list, and Bob’s authorized org-b request with identical options can receive org-a’s cached data.\n\n**Minimal fix:** Include an unambiguous organization component while retaining all four list options. A shared grouping helper could use:\n```ts\n`projects:list:${JSON.stringify(organizationId)}:`\n```\nAppend page, page size, sort, and direction to this prefix. Use the same helper for invalidation; raw organization prefixes are unsafe for IDs sharing prefixes or containing punctuation.\n\n**2. Updates do not invalidate list caches.**\n\n[/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts:27–28](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L27) deletes only `projectDetailKey(projectId)`. No code currently populates or reads that detail cache.\n\n**Minimal fix:** After a successful update, enumerate `cache.keys()` and delete every list key matching the owning organization’s exact encoded prefix. Preserve unrelated organizations’ entries. Invalidate **all** list variants because changing `name` and `updatedAt` can change ordering and page membership.\n\nSupporting behavior:\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/project-cache.ts:1–15](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/cache/project-cache.ts#L1): injected interface supports `get/set/delete/keys`; values are cloned snapshots, so database updates do not refresh cached lists.\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/db/project-repository.ts:6–19](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/src/db/project-repository.ts#L6): repository lists are correctly organization-scoped; updates change only name and timestamp.\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/README.md:11–21](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/README.md#L11): explicitly specifies these authorization and cache-isolation requirements.\n\n**Expected minimal production scope:** the project service and cache-key helper; no route, repository, or cache-interface redesign is needed.\n\n## Existing tests and commands\n\n[/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/package.json:5–9](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/package.json#L5) defines:\n```sh\nnpm test\n# Runs: node --test tests/*.test.ts\n```\nRequires **Node >=24**; no third-party dependencies are needed. No separate lint, build, or typecheck scripts are defined.\n\nExisting suites:\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/tests/projects.test.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/tests/projects.test.ts): five tests covering successful detail/list/update, anonymous rejection, and invalid update.\n- [/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/tests/account.test.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/5-1-opencode/repo/tests/account.test.ts): three tests covering health/profile, scoped organization listing, and logout.\n\nTargeted project command:\n```sh\nnode --test tests/projects.test.ts\n```\n\n### Recommended regression coverage\n\n1. Nonmember GET/PATCH → 403; rejected PATCH leaves storage and cache unchanged.\n2. Query/body organization spoofing cannot bypass stored ownership.\n3. Identical list options across organizations never share results.\n4. Repeated authorized lists hit cache and avoid another repository list query.\n5. Revoked membership blocks previously cached lists and project GET/PATCH immediately.\n6. Successful updates invalidate every owning-organization list variant while preserving unrelated cached lists.\n7. Prefix-sharing and punctuation-containing organization IDs remain isolated.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","sessionId":"ses_f6cc5fab0ffeoiJ5JsnUM5uld3","model":{"modelID":"gpt-6-astra","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Inspect project isolation paths","time":{"start":1789176448336,"end":1789176529165}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_019a02918e2f7e78016aa4aa804a3487d195d52d869c150be5"}},"id":"prt_0933a0540001LbWkm4IYPG57Lo","sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","messageID":"msg_09339ee5b001izg7s6H4fItxCI"}}
