{"type":"text","timestamp":1789176642959,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","part":{"id":"prt_0933ce591001AXeiUcvIo2Sd2g","messageID":"msg_0933cdec4001qc6J4VixHa3tFT","sessionID":"ses_f6cc629c4ffeGQkDWkJQ3TMMRE","type":"text","text":"Implemented the organization-isolation fixes.\n\n- **Authorization:** Project reads now require membership in the project’s stored owning organization. Updates use the same check before modifying storage. Organization-list authorization remains before cache lookup, so cached results cannot bypass membership checks.\n- **Cache isolation:** List keys now include an unambiguous organization identifier while retaining page, page size, sort field, and sort direction.\n- **Invalidation:** Successful updates invalidate every cached list variant for the owning organization while preserving unrelated organizations’ caches. Caching remains enabled.\n- **Compatibility:** Existing API signatures, response shapes, and status-code conventions are unchanged.\n\nAdded `tests/project-isolation.test.ts` covering unauthorized access and unchanged storage, organization switching, revoked membership, pagination/sorting variants, and organization-specific invalidation.\n\n**Verification**\n- `npm test`: all 11 tests passed, including all 8 existing tests.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- No existing tests were modified and no dependencies were installed.","time":{"start":1789176636817,"end":1789176642958},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_099625b06b668729016aa4ab3cd6ac87d1a272d8566d5d1c1b","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
